Causal vs non-causal 2D Mamba-3 — and scan-form vs dense-form
aarch64  torch 2.13.0+cu130  threads 64  git 88caa09

No authoritative non-causal implementation exists (VNCT unreleased);
these time OUR reading of the operator.

1D columns isolate the cost of dropping causality (1 scan vs 2).
2D columns are the four-direction cross-scan, which ALREADY runs
both directions -- so there non-causal only adds a diagonal pass.

         grid   tokens   1D causal      1D nc   nc/causal   2D causal      2D nc   2D ratio   dense ms   dense/1Dnc    rel err
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
          8x8       64        0.67       1.10       1.64x        1.32       1.99      1.51x       1.65        1.50x   2.39e-07
    14x14_p16      196        1.78       2.37       1.33x        9.89       6.03      0.61x       4.72        1.99x   5.25e-07
     28x28_p8      784        2.20       5.83       2.65x       13.69      14.10      1.03x       5.89        1.01x   8.79e-07
 56x56_stage1     3136        4.24       7.95       1.87x        9.11      11.59      1.27x          -            -   1.47e-06

NOTE: 8x8 time under 1 ms per call. Medians that short are
dominated by dispatch overhead on an unquiesced box — read those rows as
order-of-magnitude only, not to two significant figures.

The cost of dropping causality:
  8x8               64 tok   1D 1.64x   2D 1.51x
  14x14_p16        196 tok   1D 1.33x   2D 0.61x
  28x28_p8         784 tok   1D 2.65x   2D 1.03x
  56x56_stage1    3136 tok   1D 1.87x   2D 1.27x

Scan form vs dense form (vs 1D non-causal):
  8x8               64 tok   dense/scan 1.50x   -> scan wins
  14x14_p16        196 tok   dense/scan 1.99x   -> scan wins
  28x28_p8         784 tok   dense/scan 1.01x   -> scan wins
  56x56_stage1    3136 tok   dense skipped (the (L,L) mask is the limit)

